 "drivingQuestion": "How did they graft the palms?",
 "outcome": "not_dialectical",
 "outcomeNote": "two explanations",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "pesachim.56a.4",
   "daf": "56a",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "מַרְכִּיבִין דְּקָלִים כׇּל הַיּוֹם וְכוּ׳. הֵיכִי עָבְדִי? אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה: מַיְיתֵי אָסָא דָּרָא וְשִׁיכְרָא דְּדַפְנָא וְקִימְחָא דִשְׂעָרֵי דִּרְמֵי בְּמָנָא דְּלָא חָלְפִי עֲלֵיהּ אַרְבְּעִין יוֹמִין, וּמַרְתְּחִי לְהוּ, וְשָׁדוּ לְהוּ לְדִיקְלָא בְּלִיבֵּיהּ, וְכׇל דְּקָאֵי בְּאַרְבַּע אַמּוֹת דִּידֵיהּ, אִי לָא עָבְדִי לֵיהּ הָכִי — צָאוֵי לְאַלְתַּר. רַב אַחָא בְּרֵיהּ דְּרָבָא אָמַר: מַנְּחִי כּוּפְרָא דִּיכְרָא לְנוּקְבְּתָא.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «They» would «graft palm trees the entire day» of the fourteenth of Nisan. The Gemara asks: «How did they perform» this grafting? «Rabbi Yehuda said: They brought fresh myrtle, strong beer» made «from the» fruit of the «laurel tree, and barley flour that was cast into a vessel, and forty days has not passed» since it was ground. «They boiled them» together «and poured» the mixture «into the core of the palm tree.» And for «any» tree «standing within four cubits of that» tree, «if they did not perform this» treatment with it, «it would immediately wither» because the tree that received the treatment would grow faster at the expense of the surrounding trees. «Rav Aḥa, son» of «Rava, said: They placed a branch of a male palm tree on the female,» and by doing so the female tree would yield fruit."
  }
 ],
